# f1 = add, f2 = early, f3 = called, f4 = the getter
# How babel and rollup hand out what a file re-exports: a getter laid by a written descriptor, not configurable. The name is not listed on the record: it is appended.
# An earlier form: the ACCESS of the definition stored "Unknown" into the field beside the change that knew the getter: the field held anything, the call by that name had an unknown callee, and the record left for unseen code.
# One place decides now, the change's road: a getter that is known flows what it returns into the field; one that is not lets anything arrive there.
# The cell is written by descriptors alone, in ONE form that is not configurable, by ONE getter and no setter, on a record that written definitions alone redefine: once laid it is that getter for ever
# (the run time ends the process where a proven half is replaced or leaves its slot). The slot may still be empty: the walk looks whether it is filled and asks nothing else.
# RUN(ACCESSORS): link accesses mechanisms=all
# ACCESSORS: accessors L1.1 getter=f4 proven once-laid
# RUN(FIELD): link fields mechanisms=all
# FIELD: "add" appended proven=undefined|f1 writers-known form=not-configurable.accessor.
# RUN(LAYOUT): link layouts mechanisms=all
# LAYOUT: layout L1 changes=[IsFrozen, GainsProperty, GetsAccessor] stays-with-compiled-code
# RUN(CALLED): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# CALLED: = IsSlotFilled {{*}}key="add" receivers=[L1] level=Proven
# RUN(GETTER): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# GETTER-NOT: testedType=f4
# RUN(SHAPE): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# SHAPE-NOT: = ShapeTest
# RUN(ANSWER): run-in-shell
# ANSWER: undefined TypeError
# ANSWER-NEXT: 11 16 3
# ANSWER-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(CHECKED): run-in-shell testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,CheckWalkAtRunTime
# CHECKED: undefined TypeError
# CHECKED-NEXT: 11 16 3
# CHECKED-NEXT: exited with 0
